        "original_id": "39feb193-05c2-5792-ac96-8bd7cee07b93",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: New Orleans, Louisiana\n- Projects: Carondelet Canal, Miami and Erie Canal\n\nFacts:\n- The Carondelet Canal was a canal in New Orleans, Louisiana, U.S.A., and it operated from 1794 into the 1920s for nearly 135 years.\n- Construction on the Miami and Erie Canal began in 1825.\n- The Miami and Erie Canal was completed in 1845.\n- The Miami and Erie Canal cost the state government $8,062,680.07 to build.",
